1
00:00:02,010 --> 00:00:03,530
我们的宇宙
Our Universe.

2
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:07,500
令人敬畏 令人费解
lt's awe-inspiring and baffling.

3
00:00:07,620 --> 00:00:10,540
从巨大的恒星爆发
From colossal explosions of stars

4
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:14,140
到怪异的粒子运动…
to the strange movements of tiny particles...

5
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:17,910
…每一个新发现
...each new discovery

6
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:20,620
似乎揭示了又一层神秘的面纱
seems to reveal another layer of mystery.

7
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:24,590
我们对我们周围世界的理解
Our understanding of the world around us

8
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:28,860
已经将我们从石器时代带到了硅石时代
has taken us from the Stone Age to the Silicon Age.

9
00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:34,900
现在坚如磐石的物理定律正在分崩离析
Now ironclad laws of physics are breaking apart.

10
00:00:35,010 --> 00:00:41,570
我们所认为的现实有可能根本就不是真实的
What we believe is reality may not be real at all.

11
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,780
人类的未来取决于我们的探索…
The future of humanity depends on our discovering...

12
00:00:46,690 --> 00:00:49,560
…宇宙究竟是如何运作的
...how the Universe really works.

13
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:55,660
科学频道 - 穿越虫洞 2x07
Science.Channel - Through the Wormhole 2x07

14
00:00:56,600 --> 00:01:01,470
空间 时间 生命本身
Space,time,life itself.

15
00:01:03,510 --> 00:01:08,030
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie Through the Wormhole.

16
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:18,010
宇宙是如何运作的？
How Does the Universe Work?

17
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:21,840
把存在看作是一张大网
Think of existence

18
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:26,420
我们全都身陷其中
as an enormous web that we're all woven into,

19
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:29,180
然而我们却无法看清全貌
but we can't see the whole thing.

20
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,250
我们只能一睹我们所处之地的一斑
We just see the patch where we are standing.

21
00:01:32,370 --> 00:01:34,620
我们无法看到全貌
We can't see the whole of reality.

22
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:38,830
不过要是我们能够看到其全貌呢？
But what if we could see it all?

23
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:40,830
要是我们能够明白
What if we could understand

24
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:45,000
整个天地是如何结合在一起的呢？
how the whole of creation joins together?

25
00:01:45,110 --> 00:01:51,340
发现这个方程式的回报将是巨大的
The rewards of finding this equation would be enormous,

26
00:01:51,450 --> 00:01:53,610
一场科学革命
a revolution in science

27
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:56,880
远超出之前的所有一切 -
far beyond anything that has come before --

28
00:01:56,990 --> 00:01:58,680
一场大跃进
a great leap forward

29
00:01:58,790 --> 00:02:01,550
将改变地球上的生命
that will transform life on Earth

30
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:05,990
确保我们作为一个物种长期存在
and ensure our survival as a species.

31
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:09,190
然而我们普通凡人所希望的不就是
But what hope do we mere mortals have

32
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:13,530
揭示宇宙隐藏的秘密
of uncovering the hidden secrets of the Universe,

33
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:16,540
知晓上帝的心思么？
of knowing the mind of God?

34
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:23,070
我记得我上学的第一天
l remember my first day of school,

35
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:26,810
那时我以为要开始学习世界
the day l was supposed to start learning about the world

36
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,210
以及它是如何运作的了
and how it works.

37
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:32,610
我走到离校舍20码处
l made it about 20 yards to the schoolhouse,

38
00:02:32,730 --> 00:02:34,520
我愣住了
then l froze.

39
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,150
我所希望的就是
What hope did l have

40
00:02:38,270 --> 00:02:41,820
了解一切 了解所有东西么？
of understanding everything or anything?

41
00:02:41,940 --> 00:02:45,960
我头皮发怵
My mind reeled.

42
00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:48,340
拔腿就跑回了家
l ran back home.

43
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:55,470
我不知道科学家是否也有同样感觉
l wonder if scientists feel much the same way.

44
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:57,890
我们知之甚少
There is so much we don't know

45
00:02:57,900 --> 00:03:01,900
为什么宇宙的运作之道是这样的
about why the Universe functions the way it does.

46
00:03:02,090 --> 00:03:04,710
试想企图去下棋
lmagine trying to play a game of chess

47
00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:07,350
而你对规则却一无所知
if you don't know the rules.

48
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:09,390
你可能会使出一些招数
You might figure out some moves,

49
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:12,390
但多数是毫无意义的
but a lot of it would make no sense.

50
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:14,990
然而 一旦你掌握了规则
Once you know the rules,though,

51
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:18,960
你就能够有目的地移动棋子了
you can begin to move the pieces with purpose.

52
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:23,530
科学是我们发现这些规则的手段
Science is our means to discover those rules,

53
00:03:23,650 --> 00:03:27,140
至今我们已经发现了其中相当一些
and so far we've revealed quite a few of them.

54
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:30,780
但若是我们得到的是错误的呢？
But what if we've got them wrong?

55
00:03:32,550 --> 00:03:36,780
在普渡大学地下隧道深处
Deep in the basement tunnels of Purdue University,

56
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:41,180
科学家吉尔.詹金斯和伊弗莱姆.菲什巴哈
scientists Jere Jenkins and Ephraim Fischbach

57
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:42,720
发现
have discovered

58
00:03:42,830 --> 00:03:46,260
有个据称是牢不可破的物理学定律
that one of the supposedly unbreakable laws of physics

59
00:03:46,370 --> 00:03:47,620
被打破了
is broken.

60
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:50,690
它始于一个谜
lt began with a mystery.

61
00:03:50,810 --> 00:03:52,830
我要出去系上一些绳子
l'll come out and set up a few tethers

62
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,230
拿上一些工具
and receive some tools,

63
00:03:54,340 --> 00:03:57,030
然后他跟着我出来
then he'll come out right after me.

64
00:03:57,150 --> 00:03:59,070
2006年12月第二周
The second week of December of 2006,

65
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:00,800
宇航员走出航天飞机
astronauts from the space shuttle

66
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,970
登上国际空间站
were up in the lnternational Space Station,

67
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:05,440
出舱的人都穿戴着E.V.A.（发泡聚合材料）
and everybody was out on an E.V.A.,

68
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:06,950
有一场太阳风暴
and there was a solar storm.

69
00:04:16,330 --> 00:04:18,890
因为宇航员全都在外面
Because the astronauts were all out there,

70
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,990
所以太阳风暴成了一大新闻
the solar storm was big news.

71
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:23,290
坐在那里看着新闻 我心想
Sitting there and watching that news story,l thought,

72
00:04:23,410 --> 00:04:24,790
哇 不会那么可笑吧
"Wow,wouldn't that be funny

73
00:04:24,910 --> 00:04:28,600
如果我看到了那出现在数据里的话
if l saw that appear in the data?"

74
00:04:28,710 --> 00:04:29,500
詹金斯所研究的
Jenkins studies

75
00:04:29,610 --> 00:04:31,830
一个强大的能量来源 是我们无法看到的
a powerful source of energy we can't see

76
00:04:31,950 --> 00:04:33,840
但它就在我们身旁 -
but is all around us --

77
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:35,470
辐射能
radioactivity.

78
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:38,140
一刻不停
Every second of every day,

79
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:41,810
太阳喷射出辐射原子雨
the Sun sprays out showers of radioactive atoms.

80
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:44,480
这些原子变化无常
These atoms are unstable.

81
00:04:44,590 --> 00:04:46,920
它们吐出能量 直至烧尽
They spit out energy until they burn away

82
00:04:47,030 --> 00:04:51,590
此过程叫做放射性衰变
in a process known as radioactive decay.

83
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:55,990
放射性衰变被认为是个随机过程
Radioactive decay is supposed to be a random process

84
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:58,930
不可能受到任何影响
that cannot be affected by anything.

85
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:01,230
在06年12月上旬,
ln early December of 2006,

86
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:03,000
我们绘制了这张图表
we're plotting this.

87
00:05:03,110 --> 00:05:04,530
那是条理想的直线
lt's a nice,straight line.

88
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:06,500
其走向完全是其该走的
lt's following exactly like it should,

89
00:05:06,620 --> 00:05:08,700
然而到了12月13日 耀斑产生了
but then on December 13th,a flare happened.

90
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:11,710
我们看到衰变实际上已经偏离了
And we see that the decay has actually departed

91
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:13,610
应该走的标准衰变线
what the standard decay line should have been,

92
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,940
它偏离了相当一段时间
and it departed it for quite some time.

93
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:18,610
那实际上是约4天的时间
This is actually the space of about four days.

94
00:05:18,730 --> 00:05:21,350
似乎是 至少看上去是
lt appeared,or so it seemed,

95
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:23,550
有什么可能改变了
that something may have been changing

96
00:05:23,670 --> 00:05:25,150
这个放射性衰变过程
this radioactive-decay process,

97
00:05:25,270 --> 00:05:27,190
其中并没有什么被认为是产生变化的
which nothing is supposed to change.

98
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:30,760
菲什巴哈 理论物理学家
Fischbach,a theoretical physicist,

99
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:34,030
苦苦思索这一发现的巨大影响
struggled with the huge implications of this finding.

100
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:37,330
掌握放射性粒子分裂的速度
Knowing how fast radioactive particles break down

101
00:05:37,450 --> 00:05:39,330
是核电
is critical for nuclear power,

102
00:05:39,450 --> 00:05:43,010
核武器 电子 医学的关键
weapons,electronics,and medicine.

103
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:47,180
难道普遍接受
Could it be that a concept so uniformly accepted

104
00:05:47,290 --> 00:05:52,050
并统领现代生活的概念是错误的？
and central to modern life was wrong?

105
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,620
对核衰变的认识中
The idea that nuclear decays

106
00:05:53,730 --> 00:05:56,150
核衰变不受外部影响的概念
cannot be influenced by an external influence

107
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:59,420
是量子物理学 核物理学
is so fundamental to so many aspects of quantum physics,

108
00:05:59,530 --> 00:06:01,520
基本粒子物理学很多方面的基础
nuclear physics,elementary-particle physics,

109
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:04,060
那种变化或许动摇了
that changing that would likely have a significant change

110
00:06:04,170 --> 00:06:06,430
我们对宇宙认识
on our understanding of the Universe,

111
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,800
以及实际应用
as well as on practical applications.

112
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:11,700
遭受了这次打击后
Still reeling from this shock,

113
00:06:11,810 --> 00:06:15,100
詹金斯和菲施巴赫发现另有奥秘
Jenkins and Fischbach uncovered another mystery.

114
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:18,110
放射性衰变不仅仅受到
Radioactive decay was not just being affected

115
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:20,110
太阳耀斑的影响
by the solar flare.

116
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:24,350
放射性粒子排放所表现出来的变化
The discharge of radioactive particles appears to change

117
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:28,090
取决于地球与太阳的距离
depending on how close the Earth is to the Sun.

118
00:06:33,070 --> 00:06:34,620
当地球距离太阳较近时
When the Earth is closer to the Sun,

119
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:36,120
1月4日左右
around January 4th,

120
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:38,430
放射性衰变的速度似乎要快些
the rate of radioactive decay seems to be faster.

121
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:42,000
距离较远时 速度似乎要慢些
And when farther away,the rate seems to be slower.

122
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:44,470
现在 我们接下来就来说明一下
Now,we can illustrate this in the following way.

123
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:45,830
我代表太阳
l represent the Sun,

124
00:06:45,950 --> 00:06:47,670
吉尔将代表地球
and Jere is gonna represent the Earth,

125
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:49,170
那个桶代表
and the bucket represents

126
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:51,250
放射性镭原子
a sample of radioactive radium atoms.

127
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:56,110
你会看到吉尔沿着椭圆走动
And you'll see that as Jere moves in an ellipse,

128
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:59,050
在1月4日前后 他离地球较近时
where he's closer to the Earth around January 4th,

129
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,550
有较多的网球抛出来
more tennis balls are thrown out,

130
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:03,930
也就是有比7月4日前后更多的粒子射出来
meaning more particles come out than happen around July 4th.

131
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,290
此种数量的小变化
This small change in numbers

132
00:07:10,410 --> 00:07:13,560
可能会带来大后果
could have big consequences.

133
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:17,470
癌症患者接受极少剂量的辐射
Cancer patients receive very tiny doses of radiation

134
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:19,700
来杀死他们的反叛细胞
to kill their rebel cells.

135
00:07:19,810 --> 00:07:23,470
如果那种辐射强度有季节性变化
lf the strength of that radiation changes seasonally,

136
00:07:23,590 --> 00:07:27,780
那他们就有可能得到或多或少的剂量
they might get too little or too much of a dose.

137
00:07:27,890 --> 00:07:31,710
掌握其中的差异就能够拯救生命
Knowing the difference could save lives.

138
00:07:31,830 --> 00:07:35,050
不过这两人的发现
But the duo's most important discovery

139
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:38,220
有可能把握人类的未来
could secure the future of the human race.

140
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:42,490
在耀斑实际发生40个小时之前
40 hours prior to the actual time of the flare,

141
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:45,790
我们看到衰变率的变化 实际上已经脱离此线了
we saw the decay rate change and actually leave the line.

142
00:07:45,910 --> 00:07:48,400
耀斑发生后
After the flare,

143
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:51,770
它开始回归该线了
it started to recover and move back toward the line.

144
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:54,440
于是 这就可能给了我们机会
So,this possibly gives us the opportunity,then,

145
00:07:54,550 --> 00:07:57,170
去预测太阳耀斑何时发生
to predict when these solar flares are happening.

146
00:07:57,290 --> 00:08:00,840
一个大的太阳耀斑可以抹去
A large solar flare could wipe out

147
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:05,210
几乎所有近3000颗绕地卫星
every one of the nearly 3,000 satellites orbiting the Earth.

148
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:08,350
刹那间 我们就失去了互联网
ln a flash,we would lose the lnternet,

149
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:12,090
GPS 电视 广播 电话
GPS,television,radio,telephones,

150
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:16,530
以及控制我们电网的系统
and the systems that control our power grids.

151
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:22,260
了解耀斑将有可能避免世界末日
Knowing a flare is coming could avert a global apocalypse.

152
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:25,470
如果这种现象是真实的 我们认为是的
lf this phenomenon is real,as we believe it is,

153
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,970
那么关键在于了解它是如何发生的
then it's essential to understand how this is happening

154
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:29,470
因为这肯定会是
because this will certainly be

155
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:31,970
更大难题的一部分 我们必须要搞明白
a part of a bigger puzzle that we must understand

156
00:08:32,090 --> 00:08:33,850
把所有的物理学整合在一块
to put all this physics together.

157
00:08:36,190 --> 00:08:39,380
我们探索浩瀚的宇宙
We're groping in the dark of the vast Universe,

158
00:08:39,490 --> 00:08:42,950
以为我们已经发现了最深奥的真理
thinking we have uncovered its deepest truths,

159
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:45,920
接着发现我们对于还有大量有待认识的
then finding we still have much to learn

160
00:08:46,030 --> 00:08:48,370
自然规律
about the rules of nature.

161
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:53,600
大自然并不会让我们轻松得手的
And nature does not make things easy for us.

162
00:08:53,710 --> 00:08:56,570
下至现实最小的层面
Down at the smallest scale of existence,

163
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:59,770
深入到怪异的量子力学世界里
deep in the weird world of quantum mechanics,

164
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:02,900
似乎有两套不同的规则
it seems to play by two different rules

165
00:09:03,020 --> 00:09:04,140
同时出现
at the same time.

166
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:09,180
我们探索其奥秘越深入
And the deeper we probe into its mysteries,

167
00:09:09,290 --> 00:09:15,150
就愈加迫使我们去探究 不光是宇宙是如何运作的
the more we are forced to ask not just how the Universe works,

168
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:18,790
而且还有什么是真实的呢
but whether anything is real.

169
00:09:23,270 --> 00:09:26,730
量子力学已经改变了世界
Quantum mechanics has transformed the world.

170
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:29,660
我们将我们多数惊人技术归功于
We owe most of our amazing technology

171
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:34,700
它解释了极小粒子的…
to its explanations of how extremely small particles...

172
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:36,840
行为举止
behave.

173
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:39,670
但是我们并不真正了解它
But we don't really understand it.

174
00:09:39,790 --> 00:09:43,750
在量子世界里 似乎啥都没道理
ln the quantum world,nothing seems to make sense.

175
00:09:43,860 --> 00:09:48,050
现实不再是…真实的
Reality stops being...real.

176
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:51,290
这个谜团是我们
This mystery is our greatest obstacle

177
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,860
揭秘宇宙最大的障碍
to unlocking the secrets of the Universe.

178
00:09:53,970 --> 00:09:56,390
若是我们能够攻克它
lf we can solve it,

179
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:59,530
我们就有可能掌握了宇宙本身的关键
we may hold the keys to creation itself.

180
00:10:08,250 --> 00:10:09,970
奥地利维也纳
Vienna,Austria,

181
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:13,380
可以说是量子力学的发源地
is arguably the birthplace of quantum mechanics.

182
00:10:13,490 --> 00:10:15,280
就在这里 你能看到
This is where you will find

183
00:10:15,390 --> 00:10:18,380
世界量子实验者中的领军人物
the leading quantum experimentalist in the world,

184
00:10:18,490 --> 00:10:21,430
安东.采林格教授
professor Anton Zeilinger.

185
00:10:23,630 --> 00:10:26,390
我首次听说量子力学的时候
When l first heard of quantum mechanics

186
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,760
我还是个学生
when l was a student,

187
00:10:27,870 --> 00:10:33,870
我当时顿时惊呆于三样东西 -
l was immediately struck by three things --

188
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:37,800
首先 它有着难以置信的数学美
first,its unbelievable mathematical beauty.

189
00:10:37,910 --> 00:10:42,300
其次 其预测功能
Secondly,by the incredible precision

190
00:10:42,420 --> 00:10:44,270
难以置信的精准
to which the predictions work.

191
00:10:44,390 --> 00:10:46,140
第三
And thirdly,

192
00:10:46,250 --> 00:10:51,490
事实上… 它没有道理
by the fact that... it doesn't make sense.

193
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:56,120
量子力学描述了构成万物的
Quantum mechanics describes the behavior

194
00:10:56,230 --> 00:11:00,360
所有微小粒子的行为
of all the tiny particles that everything is made of.

195
00:11:00,470 --> 00:11:02,660
这些知识给了我们电脑
This knowledge has given us computers,

196
00:11:02,770 --> 00:11:07,500
核电 卫星 先进的医学 -
nuclear power,satellites,advanced medicine --

197
00:11:07,610 --> 00:11:08,830
大多数的伟大技术进步
most of the great leaps forward

198
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:12,230
诞生于人类过去百年里
humanity has taken in the past 100 years.

199
00:11:12,350 --> 00:11:15,070
但是量子世界似乎与
But the quantum world seems to run contrary

200
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:18,810
我们所掌握的所有自然规律背道而驰
to everything we know about the laws of nature.

201
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:23,310
简单说 下至极小极小的物体
Simply put,down where things are very,very small,

202
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:26,950
宇宙遵循了一套不同的规则
the Universe follows a different set of rules.

203
00:11:29,430 --> 00:11:32,290
考虑到量子的非局域性现象
Consider the phenomenon of quantum nonlocality,

204
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:36,390
两个粒子能够即时分享信息
when two tiny particles instantly share information

205
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:39,460
即使隔着遥远的距离
across vast distances.

206
00:11:39,570 --> 00:11:43,130
如果有量子骰子
lf there were quantum dice,

207
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:46,800
那就意味着如果我在这里掷一个骰子
it would mean that if l throw one die here,

208
00:11:46,910 --> 00:11:49,270
它就会出现某个数字
it shows a certain number.

209
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:52,370
远距离掷出的另一个骰子
The other dice thrown at some distant location

210
00:11:52,490 --> 00:11:55,670
也会出现同样的数字
would show the same number.

211
00:11:55,780 --> 00:11:56,780
这怎么可能呢？
How can that be?

212
00:11:56,900 --> 00:11:59,330
量子力学对此描述得很好
Quantum mechanics describes it very well.

213
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:03,490
一次有一次 采林格证明了
Time and again Zeilinger has proven

214
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:06,820
无论其预测有多极端
that no matter how extreme its predictions,

215
00:12:06,930 --> 00:12:10,990
量子理论的著述甚至都认为它不该这样
quantum theory works even though it shouldn't.

216
00:12:11,110 --> 00:12:13,900
或许最终证明
And perhaps the ultimate proof

217
00:12:14,010 --> 00:12:16,730
量子力学有多么令人不安
of just how unsettling quantum mechanics can be

218
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:20,800
就像那个所谓的双缝干涉实验
is something called the double-slit experiment.

219
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:26,640
它将让你产生疑问 现实究竟是否存在
lt will make you question whether reality exists at all.

220
00:12:26,750 --> 00:12:29,540
这个简单的装置
This simple configuration

221
00:12:29,660 --> 00:12:32,180
射出叫做光子的光的粒子
shoots particles of light called photons

222
00:12:32,290 --> 00:12:37,420
每次一个经过屏幕上的这两条缝隙
one at a time through two tiny slits in a screen.

223
00:12:37,530 --> 00:12:40,320
有一个激光器产生光
There's a laser which produces light.

224
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:41,920
此光被减弱到
This light is attenuated

225
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:46,800
每次只有一个光子出现
such that only one photon at a time emerges.

226
00:12:46,910 --> 00:12:51,030
这些光子将穿过双缝装置
These photons pass through a two-slit assembly,

227
00:12:51,150 --> 00:12:54,270
我们有一个记录其图谱的摄像头
and then we have a camera which registers the pattern

228
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:57,410
在双缝装置的后面
behind the two-slit assembly.

229
00:12:57,520 --> 00:13:00,510
这样 我们所看到的是光子
So,what we see is that the photons arrive

230
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:04,450
逐个抵达屏幕 - 有些在这里 有些在那里 -
one by one on the screen -- some here,some there --

231
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:08,620
看上去很随机
and it looks pretty random.

232
00:13:08,730 --> 00:13:10,990
由于光子是逐个出现的 -
Since the photons travel one by one --

233
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:14,190
有些穿过这条缝隙 有些穿过那条缝隙 -
some through this slit,some through that slit --

234
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:16,290
你会以为它们在墙上
you would expect them to leave

235
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:18,630
留下两条条纹的图案
a pattern of two stripes on the wall,

236
00:13:18,740 --> 00:13:21,430
你就错了
and you would be wrong.

237
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:25,370
它们神秘地产生了一组条纹
They mysteriously create a band of stripes.

238
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,600
这就是你预计能看到的
This is what you would expect to see

239
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:32,010
只要一束恒定的光束射过这两条缝隙
if a constant beam of light shined through the two slits.

240
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:35,640
它就会像波那样扩散到墙面上
lt would spread across the wall like a wave.

241
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:39,050
那么 一个子弹状的光粒子怎么会
So,how can single bullet-like particles of light

242
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:40,820
产生波的图谱的呢？
create a wave pattern?

243
00:13:40,930 --> 00:13:42,580
这只能发生在
This could only happen

244
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:46,860
粒子同时穿越两条缝隙
if the particles go through both slits at the same time.

245
00:13:46,970 --> 00:13:48,120
换句话说
ln other words,

246
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:51,430
粒子同时在两个地方
the particle is in two places at once.

247
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:54,330
但是其中最怪异的就是发生在
But strangest of all is what happens

248
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:58,170
你将探测器放在缝隙旁边时
when you put detectors next to the slits.

249
00:13:58,280 --> 00:14:00,870
当光子被监视时
When the photons are being watched,

250
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:04,540
波的图谱就消失了
the wave pattern disappears.

251
00:14:04,650 --> 00:14:08,740
拿走探测器 波的图谱又重现了
Take away the detectors,and the wave pattern comes back.

252
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:15,220
这表明 我们可以改变现实行为
This suggests that we can change the way reality behaves

253
00:14:15,330 --> 00:14:17,690
只要看着它就行了
just by looking at it.

254
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:21,020
这是否意味着现实本身
Does this mean that reality itself

255
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:24,130
并不是真实的呢？
is not real?

256
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:28,000
当今的答案是光子所走的路径
The modern answer is that the path taken by the photon

257
00:14:28,110 --> 00:14:30,470
不是现实的要素
is not an element of reality.

258
00:14:30,580 --> 00:14:35,200
我们不允许去讨论
We are not allowed to talk about

259
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:38,140
光子穿过这条或那条缝隙
the photon passing through this or this slit.

260
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:40,180
我们也不允许说
Neither are we allowed to say

261
00:14:40,290 --> 00:14:42,580
光子穿过这两条缝隙
that the photons pass through both slits.

262
00:14:42,690 --> 00:14:48,020
所有这种说法都是不恰当的
All this kind of language is not applicable.

263
00:14:48,130 --> 00:14:52,390
因而 我们就只能从量子力学中
So,do we just keep reaping the benefits

264
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:53,990
不断获益
from quantum mechanics

265
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:57,660
并打心底里接受大自然所表现出的那一套规则
and accept that,deep down,nature plays by a set of rules

266
00:14:57,770 --> 00:15:00,460
将永远是个不解之谜么？
that will forever remain a mystery?

267
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:03,260
这里有趣的信息就是
The interesting message here is

268
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:07,400
我们有量子物理学上百年了
that we have quantum physics now around for nearly 100 years,

269
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:10,140
我们还依然在探索其基本原理
and we are still working at the foundations.

270
00:15:10,250 --> 00:15:13,210
这就告诉我 一旦我们有所发现
And that tells me that when we find it,

271
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:16,340
那将绝对是个启示
it will be an absolute revelation.

272
00:15:16,460 --> 00:15:20,190
它将会是不同于我们一直所想的东西
lt will be something different from what we have been thinking.

273
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:28,160
若是量子理论家是正确的
lf the quantum theorists are correct,

274
00:15:28,270 --> 00:15:29,990
我们将永远都不会明白
we will never understand

275
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:32,690
宇宙的根本
the fundamental level of the Universe.

276
00:15:32,810 --> 00:15:36,330
我们寻求终极理论的愿望将告破灭
Our hopes of finding an ultimate theory will fail,

277
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,730
人类将会遇上无法突破的障碍
and the human race

278
00:15:37,850 --> 00:15:41,870
无法突破的障碍
will hit a roadblock it can't break through.

279
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:44,810
但若是他们错了呢？
But what if they're wrong?

280
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:47,340
若是这一切的真相
What if the truth about what happens

281
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:50,040
深藏在你我
deep inside you,me,

282
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:52,350
以及宇宙万物之中
and everything else in the Universe

283
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:56,230
我们是否愿意去寻求它呢？
is there if we're willing to look for it?

284
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:02,020
在20世纪大部分时间里
For most of the 20th century,

285
00:16:02,140 --> 00:16:06,030
科学家认为量子物理学是无法解释的
scientists believed quantum physics could not be explained,

286
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:08,130
我们只能接受
that we would just have to accept

287
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:11,100
我们将永远不会知道在现实的最小层面上
that we'll never know why things behave as they do

288
00:16:11,210 --> 00:16:14,300
为何事物会表现出它们的举动
down at the deepest levels of existence.

289
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:18,240
然而现在有越来越多的反叛科学家认为
But now a growing band of rebel scientists thinks

290
00:16:18,350 --> 00:16:21,140
或许最终我们能合乎逻辑的解释
there may be a logical explanation

291
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:23,710
量子的怪异
for quantum weirdness after all

292
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:26,180
有新的希望来揭示
and new hope for revealing

293
00:16:26,290 --> 00:16:30,690
我们宇宙的终极真理
the ultimate truth of our Universe.

294
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:34,960
线索始于这里…
The trail begins here...

295
00:16:35,070 --> 00:16:38,460
一滴硅
with a drop of silicon.

296
00:16:38,570 --> 00:16:39,990
在他的巴黎实验室里
ln his Paris laboratory,

297
00:16:40,110 --> 00:16:43,500
物理学家伊夫.库代及其团队
physicist Yves Couder and his team

298
00:16:43,610 --> 00:16:46,670
开展了一系列惊人的实验
conduct an amazing series of experiments.

299
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:50,370
他们观察到硅滴在震动板上步调一致
They are observing the behavior of silicon droplets

300
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:55,240
弹跳的举动
bouncing in lockstep on a vibrating plate.

301
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:56,950
滴落的液体
The liquid of the drop

302
00:16:57,060 --> 00:16:59,350
从来不会接触到基板的液体
never touches the liquid of the substrate.

303
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:01,520
它们总是被一层薄膜给分开
So,they're always separated by a film.

304
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:02,920
事实上 它是稳定的
And,in fact,it is stable.

305
00:17:03,030 --> 00:17:05,920
你可以保持硅滴在液面上弹跳上几天
You can keep the drop bouncing on the liquid surface

306
00:17:06,030 --> 00:17:07,970
只要你愿意
for several days if you wish.

307
00:17:11,610 --> 00:17:15,900
利用每秒千帧的摄像机
Using a camera that shoots 1,000 frames per second,

308
00:17:16,010 --> 00:17:18,770
库代发现这些硅滴
Couder has discovered that these droplets

309
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:22,670
酷似量子世界里所见到的举动
mimic behavior seen in the quantum world.

310
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:25,940
那应该是不可能的
And that shouldn't be possible,

311
00:17:26,050 --> 00:17:29,440
因为量子世界和大尺度世界
because the quantum world and the large-scale world

312
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:31,860
分别是两套全然不同的规则
play by two different sets of rules.

313
00:17:39,770 --> 00:17:42,720
然而我们现在看到硅滴的随机移动
Yet here we see a single droplet moving randomly

314
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:44,730
宛如量子粒子一般
like a quantum particle,

315
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:48,630
但其动作却如量子波那样
but behaving like a quantum wave.

316
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:51,330
你仔细观察 会注意到那波
lf you watch this carefully,you'll notice that the wave

317
00:17:51,450 --> 00:17:53,910
似乎在引导着硅滴
appears to be guiding the droplet.

318
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:00,680
事实上 硅滴周围的波场
ln fact,the wave fields around the droplets

319
00:18:00,790 --> 00:18:03,980
开发了硅滴所走路径的记忆
develop a memory of the trails they have followed.

320
00:18:04,090 --> 00:18:05,980
尽管其行动随意
Despite their random behavior,

321
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:08,480
但它们遵循的路径很少
they follow a small number of paths.

322
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:11,950
此外 这诡异地类似于
Again,this is eerily similar

323
00:18:12,070 --> 00:18:15,060
量子物体的动作
to the behavior of quantum objects.

324
00:18:15,170 --> 00:18:18,260
此种举动严重背离了普遍的看法
This runs so contrary to popular belief

325
00:18:18,370 --> 00:18:23,200
所以一开始 库代难以相信自己的所见
that,at first,Couder refused to believe what he was seeing.

326
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:25,400
在任何物理实验中
ln any physics experiment,

327
00:18:25,510 --> 00:18:29,070
你只看你准备看的东西
you only see what you are prepared to see.

328
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:31,310
当然 这显然存在着惯性思维
Of course,it was very obvious that there was a memory,

329
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:33,210
不过它让我们费了一点时间认识到
but it took us some time to realize

330
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,310
它就是我们所观察到的
that it was that that we were observing,

331
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:39,380
因为你得去适应这种新概念
because you have to adapt to this new idea.

332
00:18:39,490 --> 00:18:41,420
或许整个最直观的是
Perhaps most revealing of all,

333
00:18:41,530 --> 00:18:46,050
库代用其弹跳的硅滴
Couder has reproduced the double-slit experiment

334
00:18:46,170 --> 00:18:49,460
再现了双缝实验
using his bouncing silicon droplets.

335
00:18:49,570 --> 00:18:52,330
量子力学的奥秘在于
The mystery of quantum mechanics is,

336
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:54,400
电子之类的东西怎么会
how can things like electrons

337
00:18:54,510 --> 00:19:00,200
其举止有时像粒子 有时像波的呢？
sometimes behave like particles and sometimes behave like waves?

338
00:19:00,310 --> 00:19:03,500
或许这就是答案
Perhaps this is the answer.

339
00:19:03,620 --> 00:19:07,680
它们既是粒子又是波
They are particles and waves.

340
00:19:07,790 --> 00:19:13,050
当然 此种系统 虽然小 但不是量子
Of course,this system,though small,is not quantum.

341
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:15,680
我们的系统并不是量子力学的模型
Our system is not a model of quantum mechanics,

342
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:18,920
但它是粒子和波的结合
but is an association of a particle and a wave.

343
00:19:19,030 --> 00:19:22,320
其某些属性类似于
And some of its properties are similar

344
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:24,530
我们在量子力学所看的属性
to the properties that are observed in quantum mechanics.

345
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:28,460
库代并不主张他的实验向我们展现了
Couder won't claim that his experiments show us

346
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:30,300
那真的就发生在
what is really happening

347
00:19:30,410 --> 00:19:33,700
现实的最深层
down at the deepest layers of existence.

348
00:19:33,810 --> 00:19:35,740
但此人就这么认为
But this man will.

349
00:19:35,850 --> 00:19:39,170
在他看来 那些硅滴更加证明了
To him,those droplets are more proof

350
00:19:39,290 --> 00:19:41,810
归根结底是量子世界产生了意识
that the quantum world makes sense after all

351
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:45,860
那是实实在在的事实
and that reality really exists.

352
00:19:48,760 --> 00:19:52,890
克莱姆森大学的安东尼.瓦伦蒂尼
Antony Valentini of Clemson University

353
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,160
是个量子极端分子
is a quantum heretic.

354
00:19:55,270 --> 00:19:56,960
他大声宣布
He loudly proclaims

355
00:19:57,070 --> 00:20:00,330
物理学在上世纪20年代就已经出轨了
that physics went off the rails in the 1920s

356
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:03,560
当时它已经接受了量子不确定性的学说
when it embraced the doctrine of quantum uncertainty,

357
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:07,070
其声称啥都不是真实的 除非我们观察它
which says that nothing is real until we look at it.

358
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:10,840
瓦伦蒂尼捍卫着其留下的理论
Valentini champions the theory that got left behind.

359
00:20:10,950 --> 00:20:13,340
其创始人是20世纪早期的
lt was created by one of the pillars

360
00:20:13,450 --> 00:20:15,840
物理学顶梁柱之一
of early 20th-century physics,

361
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:18,210
德布罗意
Louis De Broglie.

362
00:20:18,330 --> 00:20:19,950
德布罗意最初的想法是
Louis De Broglie's original idea is

363
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:25,550
电子自始自终既是波又是粒子
an electron is both a wave and a particle all the time.

364
00:20:25,670 --> 00:20:28,560
并不是有时是粒子
lt's not the case that,well,sometimes it's a particle,

365
00:20:28,670 --> 00:20:30,090
有时是波
sometimes it's a wave.

366
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:34,800
始终就是波引导着粒子
There is a wave guiding a particle at all times.

367
00:20:34,910 --> 00:20:37,970
德布罗意称其为导波
And De Broglie called this a pilot wave.

368
00:20:38,080 --> 00:20:40,300
在量子理论中
ln quantum theory,

369
00:20:40,410 --> 00:20:44,410
有种东西叫做概率波
there's something called the probability wave,

370
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:48,180
纯数学的对象 它告诉你
a purely mathematical object that tells you the chance

371
00:20:48,290 --> 00:20:51,480
在空间任意点找到电子的机会
of finding an electron at any point in space.

372
00:20:51,590 --> 00:20:52,880
导波理论
Pilot wave theory

373
00:20:52,990 --> 00:20:57,360
将这种波看作是真正的物理对象
treats this wave as a real physical object.

374
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:05,290
简单的比喻是个瓶子
So,a simple analog is a bottle.

375
00:21:05,410 --> 00:21:08,530
有人在岛上 他们想传递信息
Someone is on an island,and they want to send a message.

376
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:11,030
他们把事情写在一张纸上
So they write something on a piece of paper,

377
00:21:11,150 --> 00:21:14,880
将纸放在瓶子里 塞住瓶口 将它扔进大海
put it in a bottle,close it,and throw it in the ocean.

378
00:21:17,790 --> 00:21:23,910
海浪推着瓶子往前
And water waves simply push the bottle along.

379
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:26,380
有个关键的区别存在于
There is a crucial difference

380
00:21:26,490 --> 00:21:30,450
我们所知的波浪与导波之间
between the waves we know and the pilot wave.

381
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:32,650
根据这个理论
According to the theory,

382
00:21:32,770 --> 00:21:36,120
导波存在于看不见的空间维度里
pilot waves exist in hidden dimensions of space

383
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:39,330
超出了我们所知的三维
beyond the three we know.

384
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:42,300
如果属实 这就意味着
lf true,this means that,

385
00:21:42,410 --> 00:21:45,400
违背了物理理论上所接受的
contrary to the accepted theory in physics,

386
00:21:45,510 --> 00:21:49,370
量子物体遵守着大物体同样的规则
quantum objects obey the same rules as large objects.

387
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:52,370
它们并不会同时处在两个地方
They do not exist in two places at once.

388
00:21:52,490 --> 00:21:55,310
它们是现实世界的组成部分
They're part of the real world.

389
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:58,410
我认为量子力学本身
l think that quantum mechanics itself

390
00:21:58,530 --> 00:22:00,310
甚至都不是
is not even a candidate

391
00:22:00,430 --> 00:22:03,780
微观世界真理的候选者
for the truth about the microscopic world,

392
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:06,490
因为它根本就没尝试精确描述
because it simply doesn't attempt to describe

393
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:08,690
微观世界是什么
precisely what the microscopic world is.

394
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:11,990
只是事实上存在着不同的说法而已
The mere fact that there are different theories

395
00:22:12,110 --> 00:22:14,200
答案或许就是
about what the answer might be

396
00:22:14,310 --> 00:22:17,100
并不意味着没有答案
doesn't mean that there's no answer.

397
00:22:17,210 --> 00:22:19,830
最终其中一个发现成了正确的答案
And eventually one of them is found to be the correct one.

398
00:22:19,950 --> 00:22:23,740
为了了解宇宙的运作
To understand how the Universe works,

399
00:22:23,850 --> 00:22:25,970
我们需要解开
we need to unlock

400
00:22:26,090 --> 00:22:28,840
为什么量子世界完全迥异于
why the quantum world is so different

401
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:31,710
我们所了解的世界
from the world we know.

402
00:22:31,830 --> 00:22:33,680
它是一个未解之谜
lt is an unsolved mystery

403
00:22:33,790 --> 00:22:36,680
影响着地球上的每一个人
that affects every single person on Earth,

404
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:41,060
此人认为他可以解决它
and this man thinks he can solve it.

405
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:49,600
我们越多了解宇宙内部的运作
The more we understand the inner workings of the Universe,

406
00:22:49,710 --> 00:22:52,930
我们就回报得到越多的新医药
the more we humans are rewarded with new medicines,

407
00:22:53,050 --> 00:22:54,170
新科技
new technologies,

408
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:57,740
以及梦想不及的生活改善
and undreamed of improvements in our lives.

409
00:22:57,850 --> 00:23:00,240
不过有人说我们揭开宇宙最深层的秘密
But some say we're a long way off

410
00:23:00,350 --> 00:23:03,540
还有很长的路要走
from unlocking the Universe's deepest secrets.

411
00:23:03,660 --> 00:23:06,410
我们要明确的答案
We want definitive answers.

412
00:23:06,530 --> 00:23:11,590
我们看到的是谜团重重
What we have are mysteries upon mysteries.

413
00:23:13,530 --> 00:23:16,090
最大的谜团之一
And one of the greatest mysteries

414
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:17,890
就是宇宙间的大东西与小东西
is how the big stuff

415
00:23:18,010 --> 00:23:20,910
是如何组合在一起的
and the small stuff in the Universe fit together.

416
00:23:23,710 --> 00:23:28,400
有两个行之有效的理论描述了物质的行为 -
Two well-tested theories describe how matter behaves --

417
00:23:28,520 --> 00:23:29,700
相对论
relativity theory,

418
00:23:29,820 --> 00:23:32,370
它负责宏观物理学
which governs the physics of the large,

419
00:23:32,490 --> 00:23:36,540
量子理论 它描述了微观
and quantum theory,which describes the very small.

420
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:41,020
如果它们是一对情侣 那相对论就是思维严谨
lf they were a couple,relativity would be a logical,

421
00:23:41,130 --> 00:23:43,180
身穿防护服的工程师
pocket-protector-wearing engineer

422
00:23:43,300 --> 00:23:47,020
他严守光速限制
who strictly follows the speed limit of light.

423
00:23:47,130 --> 00:23:49,760
量子理论则是他随心所欲的艺术家老婆
Quantum theory would be his volatile artist wife

424
00:23:49,870 --> 00:23:51,890
她似乎同时无处不在
who seems to be everywhere at once.

425
00:23:52,010 --> 00:23:54,530
理论上 它们难以相处
On paper,they don't get along.

426
00:23:54,640 --> 00:23:58,800
但是在现实世界里 它们是幸福的伴侣
But in the real world,they are a happy pair.

427
00:23:58,910 --> 00:24:01,100
就像现实生活中某些奇怪的夫妇一样
And like some real-life odd couples,

428
00:24:01,220 --> 00:24:04,170
无人明白为什么
no one understands why.

429
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:08,480
谜团归结到引力
The mystery boils down to gravity.

430
00:24:08,590 --> 00:24:11,180
引力支配着我们所知的世界
Gravity dominates the world we know,

431
00:24:11,290 --> 00:24:13,780
多亏了牛顿和爱因斯坦
and thanks to Newton and Einstein,

432
00:24:13,890 --> 00:24:16,820
我们对其已相当了解了
we understand it pretty well.

433
00:24:16,930 --> 00:24:20,220
但物理学家并不知道引力在量子领域里
But physicists have no idea what role gravity plays

434
00:24:20,330 --> 00:24:21,990
扮演了何种角色
in the quantum realm

435
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:25,260
即它对时空有何影响
or its effect on space and time.

436
00:24:25,370 --> 00:24:27,400
如果我们破解了此谜
lf we crack this mystery,

437
00:24:27,510 --> 00:24:30,770
那我们将最终知道是否有可能
we will finally know if it is possible

438
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:37,510
回到过去或穿越虫洞了
to travel back in time or through a wormhole.

439
00:24:37,620 --> 00:24:41,940
彼得.霍扎瓦长期探索
Petr Horava has a history of exploring

440
00:24:42,060 --> 00:24:45,150
未开发的物理学前沿
the wild frontier of physics.

441
00:24:45,260 --> 00:24:49,750
现在他在全力解决量子引力
Now he's tackling quantum gravity.

442
00:24:49,860 --> 00:24:53,090
你如何去调和量子力学与引力呢？
So,how do you reconcile quantum mechanics and gravity?

443
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:55,760
可以有若干不同的方式
There are several different ways it can happen.

444
00:24:55,870 --> 00:24:58,390
无论量子力学有多厉害
Either quantum mechanics is stronger and wins

445
00:24:58,510 --> 00:25:00,160
引力得作出调整
and gravity has to be modified,

446
00:25:00,270 --> 00:25:03,060
或者量子力学得作出调整
or quantum mechanics has to be modified

447
00:25:03,180 --> 00:25:06,440
引力都是与爱因斯坦的广义相对论平起平坐的
and gravity stays the same as in Einstein's general relativity.

448
00:25:08,650 --> 00:25:11,140
彼得认为 关键在于
Petr feels the key is

449
00:25:11,250 --> 00:25:13,110
观察在自然界的上层 -
to watch how things change in scale

450
00:25:13,220 --> 00:25:15,080
事物变化的规模
between the upper layers of nature,

451
00:25:15,190 --> 00:25:17,340
引力称霸的地方
where gravity holds sway,

452
00:25:17,460 --> 00:25:21,150
与下面的量子层面之间的变化
and the quantum layers down below.

453
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:24,850
大自然自身组织起了层层结构
Nature organizes itself in layers of structure,

454
00:25:24,970 --> 00:25:29,020
随之放大你看到越来越多的层面
and you see more and more layers as you zoom in

455
00:25:29,140 --> 00:25:33,990
获得更好的分辨率让你去观察这个系统
and gain a better resolution of how you view the system.

456
00:25:34,110 --> 00:25:36,200
它是现代物理学里
lt's one of the most important theoretical concepts

457
00:25:36,310 --> 00:25:37,500
最重要的理论概念之一
in modern physics.

458
00:25:39,850 --> 00:25:42,470
对于彼得来说 大自然是个考古发掘
To Petr,nature is an archaeological dig

459
00:25:42,580 --> 00:25:46,410
让我们逐层逐层慢慢发掘
that we're slowly excavating layer by layer.

460
00:25:46,520 --> 00:25:50,080
眼下 我们只能够发掘庞大而复杂的
Right now,we're only capable of uncovering a small part

461
00:25:50,190 --> 00:25:52,810
终极真理的一小部分
of the vast and complex ultimate truth.

462
00:25:52,930 --> 00:25:55,120
但是我们能够
But we can learn a lot

463
00:25:55,230 --> 00:25:57,560
通过比较我们所能见到的层次学到很多
by comparing the layers we can see.

464
00:26:02,870 --> 00:26:05,290
在这幅画里 蒙娜丽莎的两幅图像
ln this picture,the two images of Mona Lisa

465
00:26:05,410 --> 00:26:07,660
表现了时空的两面 -
represent the two faces of space-time --

466
00:26:07,770 --> 00:26:09,490
空间和时间
space and time.

467
00:26:09,600 --> 00:26:10,600
我们在大尺度上看
They look the same

468
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:12,700
它们是一样的
when we look at it at large scales,

469
00:26:12,810 --> 00:26:15,170
但一旦我们放大
but perhaps when we zoom in

470
00:26:15,280 --> 00:26:18,540
在很小的尺度上看这个系统
and look at the system at much smaller scales,

471
00:26:18,650 --> 00:26:20,910
它呈现的空间和时间的尺度
it could be that space and time scale

472
00:26:21,020 --> 00:26:22,740
迥然不同
in a very different way.

473
00:26:22,860 --> 00:26:25,650
这可能就是量子引力之谜
This could be the missing piece of the puzzle

474
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:26,910
缺失的部分
of quantum gravity.

475
00:26:27,030 --> 00:26:29,850
彼得觉得 在你缩小至
Petr suspects that as you shrink down

476
00:26:29,960 --> 00:26:33,150
现实的最小最深层面的过程中
to the smallest and deepest level of existence,

477
00:26:33,270 --> 00:26:36,790
空间开始扩张 其速率不同于时间
space begins to stretch at a different rate from time

478
00:26:36,900 --> 00:26:40,630
直至两者分裂为止
until they tear apart.

479
00:26:40,740 --> 00:26:43,460
把时空看做类似于这张纸
Think of space-time as analogous to this sheet of paper.

480
00:26:43,580 --> 00:26:45,530
在微观尺度上
At microscopic scales,

481
00:26:45,650 --> 00:26:48,300
它是平滑 几何 二维的
it's smooth and geometric,two-dimensional.

482
00:26:48,420 --> 00:26:53,510
但如果你将纸撕成两半
But if you tear the piece of paper into two halves

483
00:26:53,620 --> 00:26:55,640
看纸的边缘 -
and look at the edge of the paper --

484
00:26:55,760 --> 00:26:59,250
放大 缩小 -
zoom in,zoom out --

485
00:26:59,360 --> 00:27:01,320
其结构类似于本身
the structure is similar to itself,

486
00:27:01,430 --> 00:27:03,220
但你不妨在水平方向展开
but only if you stretch in the horizontal direction

487
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:04,490
其速率不同于
with a different rate

488
00:27:04,600 --> 00:27:07,220
你在垂直方向的展开
than when you stretch with a vertical direction.

489
00:27:07,330 --> 00:27:10,490
远处看 裂口看上很平滑
From a distance,the tear looks smooth.

490
00:27:10,600 --> 00:27:12,790
但凑近
But close up,

491
00:27:12,910 --> 00:27:15,700
你可以看到边缘的高低不平了
you can see mountains and valleys along the edge.

492
00:27:15,810 --> 00:27:19,100
同样 从远处 空间和时间
Similarly,space and time seem perfectly joined

493
00:27:19,210 --> 00:27:20,400
似乎结合完美
from a distance.

494
00:27:20,510 --> 00:27:24,070
但凑近 你可以看到它们的分离
But close up,you can see the separation.

495
00:27:24,180 --> 00:27:28,040
彼得认为时空在微观层面的分裂
Petr thinks this tearing apart of time and space

496
00:27:28,160 --> 00:27:30,980
恰是量子力学所表现出的
at the microscopic scale is precisely why

497
00:27:31,090 --> 00:27:35,950
怪异规则的原因所在
the strange rules of quantum mechanics emerge.

498
00:27:36,060 --> 00:27:39,520
如果时空错乱了
lf space and time are unhinged,

499
00:27:39,630 --> 00:27:43,760
那么粒子就无法在特定的时间处在特定的地方
particles can't be in a specific place at a specific time.

500
00:27:43,870 --> 00:27:48,160
因而 不明确 不确定
Hence,fuzziness and uncertainty.

501
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:50,900
揭开量子引力之谜
Unraveling the enigma of quantum gravity

502
00:27:51,010 --> 00:27:52,830
是我们寻求
is a major hurdle in our quest

503
00:27:52,950 --> 00:27:56,170
了解宇宙运作的主要障碍
to understand how the Universe works.

504
00:27:56,280 --> 00:27:58,870
不过它面对人类所面临的
But it shrinks against the magnitude

505
00:27:58,990 --> 00:28:02,840
最大的谜团的规模退缩了
of the biggest mystery facing humanity.

506
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:07,950
95%的宇宙正在失踪
95% of the Universe is missing.

507
00:28:08,060 --> 00:28:12,830
这个女人或许知道它在哪里 又是怎么回事
This woman may know where and what it is.

508
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:20,230
我们层层剥开大自然越多
The more we peel away the layers of nature,

509
00:28:20,340 --> 00:28:25,630
我们就越是意识到有东西在失踪 -
the more we realize that something is missing --

510
00:28:25,750 --> 00:28:27,700
事情大了
something big.

511
00:28:27,810 --> 00:28:29,940
有大量的宇宙
An enormous chunk of the Universe

512
00:28:30,050 --> 00:28:32,070
似乎不见了
seems to be invisible.

513
00:28:32,190 --> 00:28:36,640
我们无论如何都看不见 听不到 发现不了它
We can't see it,hear it,or detect it in any way.

514
00:28:36,760 --> 00:28:40,650
但如果我们想解开宇宙之谜
But if we want to unlock the secrets of the Universe,

515
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:43,520
我们想作为一个物种往前推进的话
if we want to advance as a species,

516
00:28:43,630 --> 00:28:47,070
我们就必须查明它是什么 又在哪里
we have to find out what and where it is.

517
00:28:51,170 --> 00:28:54,660
宇宙始于大爆炸
The Universe began with the Big Bang,

518
00:28:54,780 --> 00:28:58,970
原始能量的惊天大爆发
a shattering explosion of raw energy.

519
00:28:59,080 --> 00:29:04,340
那种能量以大量的超高温等离子体喷出
That energy burst outward in a mass of superheated plasma.

520
00:29:04,450 --> 00:29:07,140
随着冷却 它逐步凝聚成
As it cooled,it began to clump together

521
00:29:07,250 --> 00:29:09,940
宇宙间的所有的原料 -
into all the material in the Universe --

522
00:29:10,060 --> 00:29:15,520
构成万物的固体 液体 气体
the solids,liquids,and gases that everything is made of.

523
00:29:15,630 --> 00:29:19,690
要破解奠定我们宇宙的宇宙密码
To crack the cosmic code that underlies our Universe,

524
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:24,460
我们就必须了解各种形式的能量
we have to understand energy in all its forms.

525
00:29:24,570 --> 00:29:27,800
但如果95%的宇宙
But what if almost 95% of the Universe

526
00:29:27,910 --> 00:29:31,070
其构成的能量形式是我们看不见
is made of a form of energy we can't see

527
00:29:31,180 --> 00:29:33,330
不清楚的 咋办呢？
and don't understand?

528
00:29:33,450 --> 00:29:36,170
此类问题
These are the kinds of questions

529
00:29:36,280 --> 00:29:39,310
在瑞士的日内瓦每天都得面对
confronted daily in Geneva,Switzerland,

530
00:29:39,420 --> 00:29:42,410
那里有世界上最大的粒子加速器 -
the home of the world's largest particle accelerator --

531
00:29:42,520 --> 00:29:44,610
大型强子对撞机 -
the Large Hadron Collider --

532
00:29:44,720 --> 00:29:48,290
以及数百名物理学家
and also hundreds of physicists.

533
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:55,990
克莱尔.伯雷奇是其中的一员 但她绝不是典范
Clare Burrage is one of them,but she's hardly typical.

