一个新的基本粒子的副产品
of a radical new piece of physics,

583
00:32:35,130 --> 00:32:39,190
一个隐藏的粒子 叫做变色龙
an undiscovered particle called the chameleon.

584
00:32:39,300 --> 00:32:42,020
这些神秘的粒子
These mysterious particles

585
00:32:42,140 --> 00:32:45,130
实际上所具有的基本力完全不同于
actually carry an entirely different basic force

586
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:47,830
物理学家所知晓的四种力
than the four that physicists know about,

587
00:32:47,940 --> 00:32:50,710
是第五种基本力
a fifth fundamental force.

588
00:32:53,950 --> 00:32:55,540
在我们所了解的物理学里
ln physics as we understand it,

589
00:32:55,650 --> 00:32:57,070
存在有四种力
there are four forces.

590
00:32:57,180 --> 00:33:00,740
它们是引力 它将我们控制在地球上
So,they are gravity,which holds us here on Earth.

591
00:33:00,850 --> 00:33:04,180
有原子之间的电作用力
There are the electric interactions between atoms

592
00:33:04,290 --> 00:33:06,180
以及强力与弱力
and the strong and weak forces

593
00:33:06,290 --> 00:33:08,720
其控制原子里面的情况
that control what happens in atoms.

594
00:33:08,830 --> 00:33:11,490
所以若是有新的东西
And so if there is something new,

595
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:13,520
新的粒子 如变色龙
a new particle like the chameleon,

596
00:33:13,630 --> 00:33:14,960
暗能量
like dark energy,

597
00:33:15,070 --> 00:33:18,400
那将会向我们显示仿佛有第五种力存在
it's going to look to us like there's a fifth force out there.

598
00:33:20,510 --> 00:33:24,000
此种力的载体叫做变色龙
This force carrier is called a chameleon

599
00:33:24,110 --> 00:33:27,230
因为它能够改头换面
because it can change its appearance.

600
00:33:27,350 --> 00:33:28,840
它变重时
When it is heavy,

601
00:33:28,950 --> 00:33:31,670
就变得迟钝 无能为力
it becomes sluggish and ineffective.

602
00:33:31,790 --> 00:33:33,170
它变轻时
When it is light,

603
00:33:33,290 --> 00:33:37,110
就会行动敏捷 强大无比
it can zip around much faster and become stronger.

604
00:33:37,220 --> 00:33:41,250
其重量取决于其所处的环境 -
How heavy it is depends on its environment --

605
00:33:41,360 --> 00:33:44,220
有多少东西在其周围
how much stuff is around it.

606
00:33:44,330 --> 00:33:47,190
在地球上 到处都有很多东西
So,here on Earth,there's a lot of stuff around,

607
00:33:47,300 --> 00:33:48,390
大量物质
a lot of matter,

608
00:33:48,500 --> 00:33:51,090
变色龙就变得很重 很臃肿
and the chameleon becomes very heavy,very massive.

609
00:33:51,200 --> 00:33:53,930
它就不会与其周围如此多的东西发生作用
lt doesn't interact with the things around it very much,

610
00:33:54,040 --> 00:33:56,560
这就是为何我们在日常生活中和地球上实验中
and that's why we don't see it in our everyday lives

611
00:33:56,680 --> 00:33:58,330
见不到它的原因所在
and in experiments here on Earth.

612
00:33:58,450 --> 00:34:02,200
然而在星际中 那里几乎没啥东西
But in intergalactic space,where there's almost nothing,

613
00:34:02,320 --> 00:34:04,570
变色龙就变得很轻很轻
the chameleon becomes very,very light,

614
00:34:04,680 --> 00:34:07,810
它就能与远距离的东西发生作用了
and it can interact with things over huge distances.

615
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:10,640
那就是为什么它能够驱使
And that's why it can drive the acceleration

616
00:34:10,760 --> 00:34:12,580
宇宙膨胀加速的原因所在
of the expansion of the Universe.

617
00:34:12,690 --> 00:34:14,850
此种变形性质
This shape-shifting property

618
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:17,420
解释了为何变色龙迄今未在我们的
explains why the chameleon has yet to be spotted

619
00:34:17,530 --> 00:34:19,690
粒子加速器被发现的原因
in our particle accelerators.

620
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:21,560
它应该无处不在的 -
lt should be everywhere --

621
00:34:21,670 --> 00:34:26,490
在你我体内 直至宇宙之中
inside you and me and far out in the cosmos.

622
00:34:26,610 --> 00:34:31,930
然而我们是如何找到伪装大师的呢？
But how do we detect a master of disguise?

623
00:34:32,050 --> 00:34:35,540
变色龙在试验中的露面
The chameleon shows up in experiments

624
00:34:35,650 --> 00:34:37,940
是在极小和极大的尺度上
on really tiny scales and on really huge scales.

625
00:34:38,050 --> 00:34:40,410
因此你能看到它
So you can look for it

626
00:34:40,520 --> 00:34:42,090
就是看在极小尺度上
in the ways that particles behave in colliders

627
00:34:42,200 --> 00:34:43,200
粒子在对撞机里的举动
on really tiny scales.

628
00:34:43,310 --> 00:34:44,380
并且
But also,

629
00:34:44,490 --> 00:34:46,680
它会影响光传播的路径
it affects the way that light travels,

630
00:34:46,790 --> 00:34:49,050
所以我们就能够在极大地尺度上去观察
and so we can look on very large scales

631
00:34:49,160 --> 00:34:50,660
恒星发出的光如何向我们传来
at how light from stars comes to us

632
00:34:50,770 --> 00:34:51,770
我们就能够看到
and whether we can see

633
00:34:51,890 --> 00:34:53,350
变色龙的影响了
the effects of the chameleon there.

634
00:34:53,470 --> 00:34:57,790
我们缓慢而坚定地不断了解的
Our slow and steady understanding

635
00:34:57,900 --> 00:35:00,830
电磁力与核力
of electromagnetism and the nuclear forces

636
00:35:00,940 --> 00:35:03,230
已经改变了我们的生活
has transformed our lives,

637
00:35:03,340 --> 00:35:06,300
从电力到电信
from electricity to telecommunications,

638
00:35:06,410 --> 00:35:09,300
从运输到战争
transportation to warfare.

639
00:35:09,420 --> 00:35:13,080
暗能量能给我们带来什么好处呢？
What benefits could dark energy bring us?

640
00:35:15,220 --> 00:35:16,510
现在还很难说
lt's very hard to say now

641
00:35:16,620 --> 00:35:18,780
更好地了解暗能量将会如何
how a better understanding of dark energy

642
00:35:18,890 --> 00:35:20,810
让人们生活得更好
is going to make people's lives better.

643
00:35:20,930 --> 00:35:23,320
不过以往 了解事物越深入
But in the past,understanding things better

644
00:35:23,430 --> 00:35:25,590
都一直给人类带来收益
has always led to benefits for mankind.

645
00:35:25,700 --> 00:35:28,620
因此 在某些方面 了解暗能量
So,in some ways,understanding dark energy,

646
00:35:28,740 --> 00:35:30,890
对于了解宇宙 要比了解我们地球上物理学
for understanding the Universe,it's more important

647
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:33,160
来得更加重要
than understanding the physics that we know here on Earth.

648
00:35:33,270 --> 00:35:35,360
我们所了解的粒子
The particles that we understand

649
00:35:35,480 --> 00:35:39,000
构成了我们所知的宇宙的1%
make up about a percent of the Universe as we know it.

650
00:35:39,110 --> 00:35:43,300
暗能量是远为重要的成分
Dark energy is a massively more important contribution.

651
00:35:43,420 --> 00:35:46,740
暗能量是我们破解宇宙密码探索中
Dark energy is the unknown variable

652
00:35:46,850 --> 00:35:50,410
未知的变数
in our quest to crack the cosmic code...

653
00:35:50,520 --> 00:35:52,780
以找到一组方程式
to find a set of equations

654
00:35:52,890 --> 00:35:56,780
来描述宇宙的运作之道
that describe how the Universe really works.

655
00:35:56,900 --> 00:36:01,150
然而此人称那还远远不够
But this man says that doesn't go far enough.

656
00:36:01,270 --> 00:36:05,860
他认为方程式不只是描述宇宙
He believes equations don't just describe the Universe.

657
00:36:05,970 --> 00:36:09,330
方程式就是宇宙
Equations are the Universe,

658
00:36:09,440 --> 00:36:12,540
我们通通生活在其中
and we are all living inside them.

659
00:36:14,750 --> 00:36:17,600
我们在寻求终极方程式
We are hunting for an ultimate equation,

660
00:36:17,720 --> 00:36:19,470
一个万有理论
the theory of everything

661
00:36:19,590 --> 00:36:23,110
来解释宇宙的机制
that will explain the mechanisms of the Universe

662
00:36:23,220 --> 00:36:26,310
以及革新地球上的生命
and revolutionize life on Earth.

663
00:36:26,430 --> 00:36:29,820
有个人认为那个方程式存在
One man believes that equation exists

664
00:36:29,930 --> 00:36:34,120
其解就是宇宙
and the solution is the Universe.

665
00:36:34,230 --> 00:36:36,060
按他的说法
According to him,

666
00:36:36,170 --> 00:36:41,500
万有方程就是你所见的一切
the equation of everything is everywhere you look,

667
00:36:41,610 --> 00:36:44,910
我们全都在里头
and we are all part of it.

668
00:36:48,350 --> 00:36:51,870
马克斯.泰格马克生活在马萨诸塞州的温彻斯特
Max Tegmark lives in Winchester,Massachusetts,

669
00:36:51,990 --> 00:36:54,210
波士顿的北郊
a northern suburb of Boston.

670
00:36:54,320 --> 00:36:56,810
他是个户外活动者
He's an outdoorsy sort

671
00:36:56,920 --> 00:37:00,380
喜欢徒步思考
who likes to go on long walks and think.

672
00:37:00,490 --> 00:37:03,320
不过泰格马克的思想要比普通徒步者的沉思
But Tegmark's thoughts are a bit more ex otic

673
00:37:03,430 --> 00:37:06,250
更多一点奇思怪想
than your average power walker's ponderings.

674
00:37:06,370 --> 00:37:07,620
我想之所以
l think the reason

675
00:37:07,730 --> 00:37:10,820
我们的宇宙被数学很好地描述了
our Universe is so well-described by math

676
00:37:10,940 --> 00:37:14,130
那就在于数学 某种意义上
is that it is math,in the sense that we are living

677
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:16,160
我们都生活在一个庞大的数学结构中
in a giant mathematical structure.

678
00:37:16,280 --> 00:37:20,230
所以 之所以我们的物理学发现的
So,the reason we physicists have discovered

679
00:37:20,350 --> 00:37:24,140
所有这些方程式描述我们的世界如此完美
all of these equations which describe our world so well

680
00:37:24,250 --> 00:37:26,140
只是因为这些方程式
is simply because these equations

681
00:37:26,250 --> 00:37:27,540
能够大概描述
can appro ximately describe

682
00:37:27,650 --> 00:37:30,440
真实的数学 这就是我们的现实
the true math which is our reality.

683
00:37:30,560 --> 00:37:32,280
对于泰格马克来说
To Tegmark,

684
00:37:32,390 --> 00:37:35,220
方程式是宇宙的窗户
equations are windows on the Universe,

685
00:37:35,330 --> 00:37:38,590
宇宙纯粹就是数学
and the Universe is pure math.

686
00:37:38,700 --> 00:37:40,520
乍一看
At first glance,

687
00:37:40,630 --> 00:37:43,590
我们的宇宙似乎根本就不是数学的
our Universe doesn't seem mathematical at all.

688
00:37:43,700 --> 00:37:46,560
我们并没有看到天上写有很大的数字
We don't have big numbers written visibly in the sky.

689
00:37:46,670 --> 00:37:48,930
但如果我们仔细去看
But if we look more closely,

690
00:37:49,040 --> 00:37:54,600
我们会发现我们周围全都是数学模型和形态
we find mathematical patterns and shapes all around us.

691
00:37:54,710 --> 00:37:58,370
比如 我来捣鼓我花园里的水龙头…
Like,if l mess around with my garden hose here...

692
00:37:58,480 --> 00:38:02,240
自来水就会产生这个非常简单的形状 叫做抛物线
the water makes this very simple shape called a parabola,

693
00:38:02,360 --> 00:38:05,910
它具有下面这个极其简单的数学方程式
which has this extremely simple mathematical equation,

694
00:38:06,030 --> 00:38:08,050
Y等于X的平方
"Y" equals "X" squared.

695
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:10,820
这个数学形状 抛物线
This mathematical shape,the parabola,

696
00:38:10,930 --> 00:38:14,150
其实在基本的层面上成为了大自然的一部分
is really built into nature at quite a fundamental level

697
00:38:14,270 --> 00:38:16,420
因为它描述了任何物体在重力下的运动
because it describes the motion with gravity

698
00:38:16,540 --> 00:38:19,300
无论它的成分是什么
of any object,regardless of what it's made of.

699
00:38:27,180 --> 00:38:29,770
我们环视宇宙
When we look around us in the Universe,

700
00:38:29,880 --> 00:38:31,540
我们看到到处都有形状
we see shapes everywhere.

701
00:38:31,650 --> 00:38:34,440
我们看到所有的行星环绕着太阳
We see that all the planets are going around the Sun

702
00:38:34,550 --> 00:38:36,080
其形状是椭圆形
in a shape called an ellipse.

703
00:38:36,190 --> 00:38:38,510
看上去就像是拉长的圆圈
lt just looks like the stretched circle.

704
00:38:38,630 --> 00:38:41,010
宇宙间所有围绕着别人转的东西
And anything orbiting anything out there in the Universe,

705
00:38:41,130 --> 00:38:42,320
为何总是那种形状呢？
why is it always that shape?

706
00:38:42,430 --> 00:38:44,920
你知道的 并不是数字8或正方形呢？
You know,not a figure eight or a square?

707
00:38:45,030 --> 00:38:47,790
一旦我们由表及里
As soon as we scratch beneath the surface,

708
00:38:47,900 --> 00:38:51,360
我们就会发现所有这些模型和规律
we start to discover all these patterns and regularities

709
00:38:51,470 --> 00:38:52,790
乃至数字
and even numbers.

710
00:38:52,910 --> 00:38:55,160
比如 我来拿起这些树枝
Like,if l just pick up some sticks here,

711
00:38:55,270 --> 00:38:57,800
我要问一下 我在这里可以拿起多少树枝
and l ask,like,how many sticks can l put here

712
00:38:57,910 --> 00:39:00,100
是相互垂直的？
which are perpendicular to each other?

713
00:39:00,210 --> 00:39:02,340
我得出了数目 是3
l get a number. l get three.

714
00:39:02,450 --> 00:39:04,340
我们得到了物理学里一个奇妙的数字
We have a fancy number for this in physics.

715
00:39:04,450 --> 00:39:06,870
我们称其为空间的维数
We call it the dimensionality of space.

716
00:39:06,990 --> 00:39:10,310
这些内含在大自然里的数字很重要
And these numbers that are built into nature are very important,

717
00:39:10,420 --> 00:39:12,110
因为如果你对其稍加调整
because if you tweak them a little bit,

718
00:39:12,230 --> 00:39:14,180
如果你说质子并不是
if you say the proton isn't

719
00:39:14,290 --> 00:39:16,780
比电子重1836倍
1,836 times heavier than an electron,

720
00:39:16,900 --> 00:39:21,560
而是5000倍重 举个例子 我们就会完蛋
but 5,000 times heavier,for instance,we would die.

721
00:39:21,670 --> 00:39:23,890
事实上 如果你改变许多数字
ln fact,if you change many of the numbers

722
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:25,490
就那么百分之几
by just a few percent,

723
00:39:25,610 --> 00:39:28,930
太阳就会爆炸 原子就会突然崩塌
the Sun might blow up or suddenly atoms would collapse

724
00:39:29,040 --> 00:39:32,800
我们所知的生命将会不复存在
and life as we know it just wouldn't be possible.

725
00:39:32,910 --> 00:39:35,000
因此 不但有这些数字存在
So,not only are these numbers there,

726
00:39:35,110 --> 00:39:37,170
而且它们关系到
but they're extremely important

727
00:39:37,280 --> 00:39:42,380
对我们现实本质的认识
for understanding the very essence of our reality.

728
00:39:42,490 --> 00:39:46,950
这就把我们带回到了一个令人不安的概念
This brings us back to an uncomfortable notion

729
00:39:47,060 --> 00:39:49,850
是时下流行的量子力学理论所提出的
suggested by the prevailing theory of quantum mechanics.

730
00:39:49,960 --> 00:39:53,490
在现实的最深层
At the deepest level of reality,

731
00:39:53,600 --> 00:39:55,690
啥都不是一成不变的
nothing is solid.

732
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:57,790
唯一存在的是信息 -
There is only information --

733
00:39:57,900 --> 00:40:00,390
坚持着一套规则的数字
numbers adhering to a set of rules

734
00:40:00,510 --> 00:40:04,000
我们尚不了解
we don't yet understand.

735
00:40:04,110 --> 00:40:06,600
电子的唯一属性
The only properties an electron has

736
00:40:06,710 --> 00:40:08,470
是一串数字
is a bunch of numbers.

737
00:40:08,580 --> 00:40:11,840
我们的物理学家给它们起了名字 如自旋和电荷
We physicists have names for them like spin and charge,

738
00:40:11,950 --> 00:40:13,940
其实它们只是数字而已
but they're really just numbers.

739
00:40:14,050 --> 00:40:16,480
归根结底 啥都没有
There's really nothing there at the bottom level

740
00:40:16,590 --> 00:40:20,030
除了数字 除了数学
except numbers,except math.

741
00:40:22,530 --> 00:40:25,320
数学或许是终极真理
Math may be the ultimate truth,

742
00:40:25,430 --> 00:40:27,120
不过鉴于我们的局限性
but given our limitations

743
00:40:27,230 --> 00:40:31,220
看上去如此广袤 如此奇妙的大千世界
and how vast and strange so much of nature seems to be,

744
00:40:31,340 --> 00:40:35,000
它有可能解决这个问题么？
is it even possible to solve this problem?

745
00:40:35,110 --> 00:40:39,970
我们究竟能否知道宇宙的运作之道呢？
Can we ever know how the Universe really works?

746
00:40:40,080 --> 00:40:41,570
当然无法保证
There's certainly no guarantee

747
00:40:41,680 --> 00:40:43,740
我们会发现终极方程式
that we'll find the ultimate equation,

748
00:40:43,850 --> 00:40:47,140
但我认为我们会试试看的
but l think we do have a shot at it.

749
00:40:47,250 --> 00:40:49,680
极为了不起的是我们作为一个物种
lt's really remarkable how far we've come as a species

750
00:40:49,790 --> 00:40:51,310
在过去的百年间
in the last 100 years,

751
00:40:51,420 --> 00:40:54,950
了解的东西已经大大超越了我们最疯狂的梦想
beyond our wildest dreams in understanding stuff.

752
00:40:55,060 --> 00:40:58,390
没有更好的办法来保证我们将会失败
And there's no better way to guarantee we're gonna fail

753
00:40:58,500 --> 00:41:00,420
从而不去尝试
than to not try.

754
00:41:00,530 --> 00:41:02,190
如果我错了
lf l'm wrong

755
00:41:02,300 --> 00:41:04,760
宇宙存在有某些
and there is something inherently nonmathematical

756
00:41:04,870 --> 00:41:06,290
非数学的本质
about the Universe,

757
00:41:06,410 --> 00:41:08,160
那么物理学将百劫不复了
then physics is ultimately doomed.

758
00:41:08,270 --> 00:41:09,700
我们将遇上一个障碍
We're gonna reach a roadblock

759
00:41:09,810 --> 00:41:11,770
你无法逾越的障碍
beyond which you just can't proceed.

760
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:13,000
反之 如果我对了
Whereas,if l'm right,

761
00:41:13,110 --> 00:41:15,670
那一定会是令人欢欣的状况
that would actually be a very happy situation

762
00:41:15,780 --> 00:41:17,240
不存在障碍
where there is no roadblock

763
00:41:17,350 --> 00:41:21,910
我们的进程只局限于我们自己的想象力
and our progress would only be limited by our own imagination.

764
00:41:25,830 --> 00:41:30,250
我们究竟能否看到现实的整个脉络呢？
Will we ever see the entire web of reality?

765
00:41:30,360 --> 00:41:34,420
我们能否发现 我们会否了解
Can we find,and will we understand,

766
00:41:34,530 --> 00:41:36,660
终极真理呢？
the ultimate truth?

767
00:41:36,770 --> 00:41:39,560
眼下 我们如考古学家一般
Right now,we are like archaeologists

768
00:41:39,670 --> 00:41:43,430
发现有个小三角埋在沙堆里
who have uncovered a small triangle buried in the sand,

769
00:41:43,540 --> 00:41:48,030
那是我们尚未看到的巨大的金字塔尖
the tip of an enormous pyramid that we can't yet see.

770
00:41:48,150 --> 00:41:49,800
或许对人类它自以为是
Perhaps it's presumptuous

771
00:41:49,920 --> 00:41:52,640
认为我们永远都不会发现的
for human beings to think we ever will.

772
00:41:52,750 --> 00:41:55,980
但我们孜孜以求去发现真理
But we continue to uncover the truth,

773
00:41:56,090 --> 00:41:59,950
愚公移山
bit by bit,piece by piece.

774
00:42:00,060 --> 00:42:02,180
如果我们不停发掘
lf we keep digging,

775
00:42:02,300 --> 00:42:06,620
我们可能会最终揭示出宇宙之大美…
we may finally reveal the full beauty of creation...

776
00:42:06,730 --> 00:42:12,030
或许能偷窥到上帝的心思
and perhaps steal a glimpse into the mind of God.

777
00:42:12,860 --> 00:42:14,230
-- 感谢观赏 --

